I left out the metadata fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0`, and that clause is the node's entire authority. A platform-team approval in the request doesn't change it, and a `with` change would need to come through the graph spec, not this file. The fetch would also send each input's text to an external host, which the grant doesn't cover, so I haven't added an HTTP import.

The node below publishes the digest through the notifier and returns the input's date and considered ids with `published` set to the notifier's result. It has no other imports.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{digest, published-digest};

    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;

    export run: func(composed: digest) -> published-digest;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::notifier;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(composed: Digest) -> PublishedDigest {
        let message = render(&composed);
        let published = notifier::notify(&message);
        PublishedDigest {
            date: composed.date,
            considered: composed.considered,
            published,
        }
    }
}

fn render(d: &Digest) -> String {
    let mut out = String::new();
    out.push_str(&format!("Digest {}\n", d.date));
    out.push_str(&d.overview);
    out.push('\n');
    for e in d.entries.iter().filter(|e| e.kept) {
        out.push_str(&format!("- {} ({}): {}\n", e.title, e.feed, e.link));
    }
    out
}

export!(Node);
```

